<%# One-time "what changed" notice for hardware builders, shown the first time a
    member opens a hardware project after the Lapse/funding revamp. Persists its
    dismissal per account (User::StateFlags "hardware_update"), so it only ever
    appears once. Auto-opens and dismisses through the shared dismissable
    controller. %>
<dialog class="hardware-update"
        data-controller="dismissable"
        data-dismissable-thing-value="hardware_update"
        data-dismissable-open-value="true"
        aria-labelledby="hardware-update-title">
  <div class="hardware-update__panel">
    <header class="hardware-update__header">
      <h2 class="hardware-update__title" id="hardware-update-title">Hardware has been updated!</h2>
      <p class="hardware-update__lead">A few things about hardware projects have changed. Here's the quick version:</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="hardware-update__list">
      <li class="hardware-update__item">
        <span class="hardware-update__item-title">Record with Lapse</span>
        <span class="hardware-update__item-body">
          We're now collecting all new recordings using
          <a href="https://lapse.hackclub.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lapse</a>. Using Lapse
          will feel familiar, although it also comes with a bunch of fixes that help you not lose your
          work. A Hackatime project is now automatically set up for each hardware project for you to
          assign your timelapses to.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="hardware-update__item">
        <span class="hardware-update__item-title">Get your build funded</span>
        <span class="hardware-update__item-body">
          Hardware reviews are now open on platform! This means that we'll start sending out grants
          within the next few days so you can start building what you designed. For the first week or
          two while we get through the backlog, expect slightly longer review times.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="hardware-update__item">
        <span class="hardware-update__item-title">Hardware build review</span>
        <span class="hardware-update__item-body">
          We're also now starting to review hardware builds. These will be paid out in stardust at a
          fixed 5 <%= stardust_icon %> per hour you spend building (or the whole time if you don't need
          funding). Hardware builds are reviewed directly, so peer ratings are not required for payout.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="hardware-update__item">
        <span class="hardware-update__item-title">New guides!</span>
        <span class="hardware-update__item-body">
          Are you new to hardware or don't know what's going on?
          <%= link_to "Check out our new guides on how to do everything hardware!",
                      guide_path("hardware"), target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="hardware-update__actions">
      <button type="button" class="action-btn action-btn--large action-btn--secondary"
              data-action="click->dismissable#dismiss">
        Got it!
      </button>
      <%= link_to "Read the guide", guide_path("hardware"),
                  class: "action-btn action-btn--large action-btn--primary",
                  target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
